  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>As a Magic action, you can channel the Song of Creation to create one nonmagical item of your choice in an unoccupied space within 10 feet of you, on a surface or in a liquid that can support it. Its value in GP can't exceed 20 times your Bard level, and it must be Medium or smaller (Large at Bard level 6, Huge at level 14). The item glimmers softly, and a creature touching it faintly hears music. It disappears after a number of hours equal to your Proficiency Bonus.</p><p>Once you create an item with this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a level 2+ spell slot to use it again. You can have only one item created by this feature at a time; if you create another, the first one immediately vanishes.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
